-- title:
--   Node integers have residues of non-negative order at w
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a natural number $N \neq 0$, an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $q$, and a ring homomorphism $red : A \to k$. Let `data` be a modular polynomial datum at $q$ (a monic $\Phi \in \mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ of degree $\psi(q)$ annihilating the pair of $q$-expansions) and `hKr` the Kronecker congruence, i.e. the reduction of $\Phi$ modulo $q$ equals $(C(X)^q - X)(C(X) - X^q)$; let `hα`, `hβ` be the integrality hypotheses on the two degeneracy maps $\bar\alpha, \bar\beta$ from level $N$ to level $Nq$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and $P$ a place specialisation for these data. Let $R$ be a prolongation tuple over $P$, so in particular $R$ carries two regular prolongations $R_1, R_2$ of $A$ to the level-$Nq$ function field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with residues in the level-$N$ full function field over the residue field of $A$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC k N` satisfying the regularity law `R.RegularityLaw W` (an affine-place clause and a node clause for the pairs $(v, \varphi v)$, $v \in W$, where $\varphi =$ `arithFrobC q k N` is the coefficientwise Frobenius automorphism; both clauses are summarised here), let $K$ be a finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and let $w \in W$. Then for every $g$ in the subring `R.nodeIntegersOver K w` — that is, every $g$ in the level-$Nq$ function field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ which lies in the valuation subrings $R_1$.integers and $R_2$.integers and in the valuation subring of every place $V$ of that field with $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,V = w$, and whose Laurent expansion lies in the subfield generated by the constants from $K$ together with $j$ and $j_{Nq}$ — the two residues satisfy $\operatorname{ord}_w(R.\mathrm{nodeResidue}_1\,w\,g) \geq 0$ and $\operatorname{ord}_{\varphi \cdot w}(R.\mathrm{nodeResidue}_2\,w\,g) \geq 0$, where $\operatorname{ord}$ denotes minus the logarithm of the adic valuation of the place.
--
--   This records the regularity half of the local description of the node at a supersingular point of the special fibre of $X_0(Nq)$: elements of the node ring with expansions over a fixed number field are regular at both branches. It feeds the identification of the node ring with a model of a crossing $uv = \text{const}$ and the attendant unit and attachment statements.
